  "rationale": "structural: The structural obligations in `requirements.sdk.errors` are these. (1) `Domain` defines a central associated type `type Error: Send;`. An alternative would be a concrete error type, or an `Error` without the `Send` bound. Either one would violate the clause. (2) Node reads, edge queries and evidence persistence report internal errors through that `Error` type. An alternative would be an unrelated error type, or panics, in those signatures. Each root covers one obligation:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/type[Error]` declares `type Error: Send;` with the doc comment about application-defined errors. It carries `{impl}` for `requirements.sdk.errors`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/fn[node_content]` returns `Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` returns `Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/fn[load_evidence]` returns a future of `Result<Option<Record<..>>, Self::Error>`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/fn[store_evidence]` returns a future of `Result<(), Self::Error>`.\n\nAll five items are marked `{impl}` for `requirements.sdk.errors`. They match the declaration shown in the requirement text and the one in `requirements.sdk.domain`. The text names no other structural obligation. The `Clone + Send + Sync` supertrait bound belongs to `requirements.sdk.domain`, which this requirement only cites.\n\nbehavioral: `requirements.sdk.errors` states one observable obligation. `Domain::Error` is an associated type bounded by `Send` only. The Error type is used to report errors from node reads, edge queries and evidence persistence.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` is marked `{test}` for the requirement. It covers the obligation in these ways:\n- **Fixture error type.** The fixture `GraphError(Cell<u8>)` is `Send` but not `Sync`. `impl Domain for Relationships` uses it as `Error`. This shows that the trait does not demand more than `Send`. If a `Sync` bound were added, the fixture would stop compiling.\n- **Required `Send` bound.** The nested `check_bounds<G: Domain>` calls `error::<G::Error>()`, where `error<T: Send>`. Generic code therefore depends on `Send`. If the `Send` bound were removed from the trait, this would stop compiling.\n- **Evidence futures.** `check_bounds` and the test body pass `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` through `send(...)`. This shows the futures stay `Send` even though the error is not `Sync`.\n- **Error reporting by operation.** The test calls `graph.node_content(...)`, `load_evidence(...)` and `store_evidence(...)`, which return `Result<_, Self::Error>`. For edge queries, `outgoing_edges` on `Identity(255)` is asserted to return an error. The test sends that error through `send(error)` and checks that its inner value is 255.\n\nThe requirement has no other conditions, boundaries or failure cases. The `{cite}` of `requirements.sdk.domain` is context only. The whole test is already marked for the subject, so there is no marking gap.",
